(7707915, 1266324, 83313, '<td valign="top">Gotta be a Wendy shot! Those color tones aren''t your usual style of editing, though. My only slight criticism is the foreground looks a tad grainy to me. Might not even be visible on all monitors. I''d do some selective noise reduction on the smooth water in the foreground to get a nice glassy look to it. 

<br/>
<br/>Reminds me of the white balance I used in one of my own shots of a similar scene a few years back.

<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=854800" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1170/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_854800.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1170/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_854800.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1170/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_854800.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Gotta be a Wendy shot! Those color tones aren''t your usual style of editing, though. My only slight criticism is the foreground looks a tad grainy to me. Might not even be visible on all monitors. I''d do some selective noise reduction on the smooth water in the foreground to get a nice glassy look to it. 


Reminds me of the white balance I used in one of my own shots of a similar scene a few years back.

